<title>UKRAINE: Pripps Ringnes AB buys 50 pct in Ukraine brewer.</title>
<headline>Pripps Ringnes AB buys 50 pct in Ukraine brewer.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Pripps Ringnes AB brewery signed a $10 million deal to take over 50 percent of Ukraine's Slavutych beer maker, a Swedish trade official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a commitment to invest $10 million in modernising and improving the production facilities,&quot; Ulf Laurin of the Swedish Employers' Confederation, told a Swedish-Ukrainian trade conference.</p>
<p>Pripps Ringnes is owned by Norwegian food conglomerate Orkla and Swedish auto group Volvo.</p>
<p>--Irene Marushko, Kiev Newsroom +380 44 229 2264</p>
